  "id": "Compound::DB00563 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "Methotrexate is implicated in the regulation of Slc22a6 through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Methotrexate causes Cytomegalovirus Infection, which in turn binds Slc22a6, and similarly, Methotrexate causes Pneumocystis Jirovecii Pneumonia, which also binds Slc22a6. These mechanisms are supported by the shared lowest common ancestors, indicating a common biological function or pathway. The presence of carboxylic acid and enzyme inhibitor relationships further suggests a broader biochemical context in which Methotrexate influences cellular processes that ultimately affect Slc22a6. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Methotrexate in modulating Slc22a6 through viral infections and antiviral treatments, emphasizing the importance of these interactions in cellular physiology.",
